    <releaseNotes>## 2.3.0 (2026-11-26)

### New

- \#306 Azure Blob: a SAS token can be used instead of the account key (access restricted to a container, limited permissions and expiry date) - Thanks to @yenneferofvengerberg

### Fixed

- \#424, \#475 Amazon S3: saving to S3 compatible storage failed (e.g. Cloudflare R2, Synology C2)
- \#469 Amazon S3: Backup to Remote did not remove old backups if the database is stored in a folder
- \#351 Azure: adding a second Blob/File storage account replaced the first one ("This account already exists")
  _Note:_ Azure accounts added with an older version are not recognized when added again (e.g. to update the access key) - a second account is created instead. Please remove the old account in `Tools - KeeAnywhere Settings` in this case.
- \#432 Google Drive: adding an account without granting access to Google Drive (unchecked checkbox on Google's consent page) led to "Error 403: insufficient authentication scopes" later - this is now detected when adding the account
- \#290 Dropbox: clicking "Cancel" on the authorization page caused an unhandled exception (a possible exception when cancelling the authorization of Google Drive and OneDrive is fixed as well)
- Cancelling the authorization in KeeAnywhere's wait dialog did not stop waiting for the browser - a later login in the browser still added the account; closing the dialog with X did not cancel at all. Box, HiDrive: same unhandled exception as in \#290 when cancelling the authorization
- \#322, \#325, \#346 Google Drive: the file dialog crashed with "Invalid char in path" if a folder contained a file or folder whose name contains control characters (e.g. tab or newline) - such items are listed now, but can still not be opened
- \#173 Backup: other files saved beside the database (e.g. the .xml file of KeeChallenge) were backed up as .kdbx files and rotated together with the database backups - backups now keep the extension of the saved file
- Backup: saving failed if old backups could not be removed, or - with "Backup to Remote" - if the file name contained characters like `"` or `|`; old remote backups of such files were not removed
- \#420 OneDrive: adding an account without name failed - the user name or email address is used then
- \#437 Settings: the Add button could not be used with the keyboard or a screen reader
- \#490 File dialog: account dropdown was clipped with high DPI settings (e.g. 125%)
- \#330 KeePass waited forever when the connection was interrupted while saving or opening (Dropbox, Google Drive, Box, Amazon S3) - requests time out after 5 minutes now (a shorter timeout can be set per URL with KeePass' connection property `Timeout`, see [FAQ](https://keeanywhere.de/use/faq#timeout))

### Improved

- Error messages are readable now (e.g. missing permissions, wrong keys, network problems) instead of showing the complete technical exception; the details (incl. stack trace) can be expanded and copied to the clipboard for issue reports
- Authorization: the browser shows whether the authorization succeeded, was denied or failed; the wait dialog explains to click Cancel if the access was denied (e.g. Box doesn't return to KeeAnywhere in this case)
- Updated Dependencies (AWS, Dropbox)


      [Full Changelog](https://github.com/Kyrodan/KeeAnywhere/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)
    </releaseNotes>
